#: lumos.fields.wavefront:1 of
msgid "Coherent monochromatic fields sampled on a grid (REQ-SIG-2)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront:3 of
msgid ""
"A :class:`Wavefront` is the complex amplitude :math:`U(x, y)` of a "
"monochromatic field at one vacuum wavelength :math:`\\lambda`, sampled on"
" a :class:`~lumos.fields.Grid`. With the convention of §9 of the "
"specifications, the physical field is :math:`E(\\mathbf r, t) = "
"\\mathrm{Re}\\{U(\\mathbf r)\\,e^{-i\\omega t}\\}` and a wave travelling "
"towards :math:`+z` varies as :math:`e^{+ikz}` with :math:`k = "
"2\\pi/\\lambda`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront:9 of
msgid "Normalisation"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront:10 of
msgid ""
"The field is stored without units in an array of the current backend. Its"
" normalisation is a metadata, :attr:`Wavefront.power_unit` (``W`` or "
"``photon / s``), chosen such that"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront:13 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"P = \\sum_{i,j} |U_{ij}|^2\\,\\Delta x\\,\\Delta y\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront:15 of
msgid ""
"is the power carried by the field. :math:`|U|^2` is then an irradiance (W"
" m⁻²) on a spatial grid, or a radiant intensity (W sr⁻¹) on an angular "
"grid."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront:1 of
msgid "Complex scalar field at one wavelength, sampled on a grid."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront:3 of
msgid ""
"Complex amplitude, shape ``grid.shape``: any array-like. A NumPy array or"
" a list is copied into the current backend, an array of another backend "
"stays on it; the dtype follows ``lumos.config.precision``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront:6 of
msgid "Sampling of the field."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront:7 of
msgid ""
"Vacuum wavelength (a frequency or a photon energy is converted with "
"``u.spectral()``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront:8 of
msgid "Normalisation of the field: ``u.W`` (default) or ``u.photon / u.s``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle:6 lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube:10
#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront:11 of
#, fuzzy
msgid "Notes"
msgstr "Unités"

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront:12 of
msgid ""
"Wavefronts are immutable values: operations return new wavefronts. They "
"are JAX pytrees (the field is the only leaf), so pure functions of "
"wavefronts can be compiled with :func:`lumos.jit` and differentiated."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.plane:1 of
msgid ""
"Uniform, flat-phase field carrying ``power`` (in W or photon / s) over "
"the grid."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.plane:3 of
msgid ""
"``polarization`` (a Jones vector or a state name of "
":func:`lumos.fields.jones.vector`) makes a polarised field."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.gaussian:1 of
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Gaussian beam at its waist, :math:`U = \\sqrt{2P/(\\pi "
"w^2)}\\,\\exp(-r^2/w^2)`, centred on the grid."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.gaussian:3 of
msgid ""
"The intensity integrates to ``power`` over the infinite plane; the "
"sampled power differs from it only when the beam is truncated by the grid"
" or undersampled."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.field:1 of
msgid ""
"Complex amplitude, a backend array of shape ``grid.shape`` (in "
"sqrt(power_unit) / grid.unit)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.grid:1
#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.grid:1 of
msgid "Sampling grid."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.polarized:1 of
msgid ""
"Whether the field holds the Jones components ``(Ex, Ey)`` along its first"
" axis."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.with_polarization:1 of
msgid "Return a polarised copy of a scalar field, in the state ``polarization``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.with_polarization:3 of
msgid ""
"``polarization`` is a Jones vector (normalised here, so the power is "
"unchanged) or a state name of :func:`lumos.fields.jones.vector`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.shape:1
#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.shape:1
#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.shape:1 of
msgid "Shape of :attr:`field`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.backend:1
#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.backend:1
#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.backend:1 of
msgid "Name of the backend holding the field."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.wavelength:1 of
msgid "Vacuum wavelength."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.wavelength_si:1 of
msgid "Vacuum wavelength in metres."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.wavenumber_si:1 of
msgid "Vacuum wavenumber ``k = 2π/λ`` in rad / m."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.power_unit:1
#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.power_unit:1 of
msgid "``W`` or ``photon / s``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.power_unit:3 of
msgid "Normalisation of the field"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.intensity_unit:1
#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.intensity_unit:1 of
msgid "power per m² (spatial grid) or per sr (angular grid)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.intensity_unit:3 of
msgid "Unit of :attr:`intensity`"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.intensity:1 of
msgid ""
":math:`|U|^2` (:math:`|E_x|^2 + |E_y|^2` if polarised), a real "
"``grid.shape`` array."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.amplitude:1 of
msgid ""
":math:`|U|` of each component, a real backend array of the shape of "
":attr:`field`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.phase:1 of
msgid ":math:`\\arg U` of each component in radians, in ``(-π, π]``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.power:1 of
msgid ""
"Power :math:`\\sum |U|^2 \\Delta x \\Delta y` carried by the field, in "
":attr:`power_unit`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.normalized:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the field scaled to carry ``power`` (its unit becomes the power "
"unit)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.with_power_unit:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the same light expressed in another power unit, using the photon "
"energy ``hc/λ``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.tilt:1 of
msgid ""
"Multiply by the phase of a plane wave travelling at angles "
":math:`(\\theta_x, \\theta_y)` to z."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.tilt:3 of
msgid ""
"The factor is :math:`\\exp[ik(x\\sin\\theta_x + y\\sin\\theta_y)]`, null "
"at the coordinate origin; the angles are measured in the x-z and y-z "
"planes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.to_backend:1 of
msgid "Return the same field held by backend ``name``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavefront.Wavefront.to_json:1 of
msgid ""
"Encode the wavefront as a strict-JSON-compatible dictionary (the field "
"inline, in base64)."
msgstr ""

