msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube:1 of
msgid "Polychromatic fields: stacks of wavefronts on a spectral axis (REQ-SIG-4)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube:3 of
msgid ""
"A :class:`Wavecube` holds the complex amplitudes :math:`U_k` of a field "
"at the vacuum wavelengths :math:`\\lambda_k`, all sampled on the **same**"
" :class:`~lumos.fields.Grid`, with spectral weights :math:`w_k`. Its "
"field has shape ``(nλ, ny, nx)`` (scalar) or ``(nλ, 2, ny, nx)`` "
"(polarised)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube:7 of
msgid ""
"Each channel is normalised like a :class:`~lumos.fields.Wavefront`: "
":math:`P_k = \\sum |U_k|^2 \\Delta x \\Delta y` is the power carried by "
"channel :math:`k`. Fields at different wavelengths do not interfere in a "
"time-averaged intensity (Born & Wolf, *Principles of Optics*, §10.3), so "
"the detected quantities are weighted **incoherent** sums over the "
"channels:"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube:12 of
msgid ""
"I = \\sum_k w_k |U_k|^2, \\qquad P = \\sum_k w_k P_k .\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube:14 of
msgid ""
"The weights hold quadrature weights, a spectral transmission or a "
"detector response (default: 1); see "
":func:`~lumos.fields.spectral_samples` to sample a band."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube:1 of
msgid "Complex field at several wavelengths, sampled on a common grid."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube:3 of
msgid ""
"Complex amplitudes, shape ``(nλ, ny, nx)`` or ``(nλ, 2, ny, nx)`` (Jones "
"components)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube:4 of
msgid "Common sampling of every channel."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube:5 of
msgid ""
"``nλ`` vacuum wavelengths (or frequencies, converted with "
"``u.spectral()``)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube:6 of
msgid ""
"``nλ`` dimensionless spectral weights used by the integrated quantities "
"(default: ones)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube:7 of
msgid "Normalisation of every channel: ``u.W`` (default) or ``u.photon / u.s``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube:11 of
msgid "Wavecubes are immutable JAX pytrees whose only leaf is the field."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.from_wavefronts:1 of
msgid "Stack wavefronts sharing the same grid, power unit and polarisation."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.plane:1 of
msgid ""
"Uniform flat-phase field; ``power`` is the power of each channel (a "
"scalar or one per channel)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.field:1 of
msgid "Complex amplitudes, a backend array of shape ``(nλ, [2,] ny, nx)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.grid:1 of
msgid "Common sampling grid."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.polarized:1 of
msgid "Whether each channel holds the Jones components ``(Ex, Ey)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.n_wavelengths:1
#: lumos.fields.radiance.RadianceField.n_wavelengths:1
#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.n_wavelengths:1 of
msgid "Number of spectral channels."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.wavelengths:1 of
msgid "Vacuum wavelengths of the channels."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.modal.ModalField.wavelengths_si:1
#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.wavelengths_si:1 of
msgid "Vacuum wavelengths in metres."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.weights:1 of
msgid "Spectral weights of the channels (a copy)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.power_unit:3 of
msgid "Normalisation of every channel"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.intensity_unit:3 of
msgid "Unit of the intensities"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.wavefronts:1 of
msgid "Iterate over the channels as wavefronts."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.intensity:1 of
msgid "Intensity of each channel, shape ``(nλ, ny, nx)`` (polarisations summed)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.integrated_intensity:1 of
msgid "Weighted incoherent sum :math:`\\sum_k w_k |U_k|^2`, shape ``grid.shape``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.power:1 of
msgid "Power of each channel, shape ``(nλ,)``, in :attr:`power_unit`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.total_power:1 of
msgid "Weighted total power :math:`\\sum_k w_k P_k`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.with_power_unit:1 of
msgid ""
"Return the same light in another power unit, using the photon energy of "
"each channel."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.tilt:1 of
msgid ""
"Multiply each channel by :math:`\\exp[ik_k(x\\sin\\theta_x + "
"y\\sin\\theta_y)]` (chromatic tilt)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.to_backend:1 of
msgid "Return the same cube held by backend ``name``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.wavecube.Wavecube.to_json:1 of
msgid ""
"Encode the cube as a strict-JSON-compatible dictionary (the field inline,"
" in base64)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent:1 of
msgid "Sets of mutually incoherent modes (REQ-SIG-5)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent:3 of
msgid ""
"An :class:`IncoherentBundle` holds :math:`M` fields :math:`U_m` (the "
"*modes*) that are mutually incoherent: point sources of a scene, samples "
"of an extended object, coherent modes of a partially coherent beam or the"
" two orthogonal polarisations of natural light. Each mode is a "
":class:`~lumos.fields.Wavefront` or a :class:`~lumos.fields.Wavecube` and"
" all modes share the same grid, wavelengths and power unit, so the bundle"
" is one array of shape ``(M, *mode_shape)`` that elements process in a "
"single vectorised operation."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent:9 of
msgid ""
"Since the modes do not interfere (Born & Wolf, *Principles of Optics*, "
"§10.3; Goodman, *Statistical Optics*, §5.2), detected quantities are "
"**sums of intensities** with mode weights :math:`v_m` (default 1):"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent:12 of
msgid ""
"I = \\sum_m v_m I_m, \\qquad P = \\sum_m v_m P_m ,\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent:14 of
msgid ""
"where :math:`I_m` and :math:`P_m` are the (spectrally integrated) "
"intensity and power of mode :math:`m`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent:16 of
msgid ""
"A point source at infinity in the direction :math:`(\\theta_x, "
"\\theta_y)` illuminates a pupil with the plane wave "
":math:`\\exp[ik(x\\sin\\theta_x + y\\sin\\theta_y)]` "
"(:meth:`IncoherentBundle.point_sources`)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle:1 of
msgid "Mutually incoherent modes sharing a grid, wavelengths and power unit."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle:3 of
msgid ""
"Build bundles with :meth:`from_signals`, :meth:`point_sources` or "
":meth:`unpolarized`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle:7 of
msgid ""
"Bundles are immutable JAX pytrees whose only leaf is the field of shape "
"``(M, *mode_shape)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.from_signals:1 of
msgid ""
"Bundle wavefronts (or wavecubes) sharing grid, wavelengths, power unit "
"and polarisation."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.point_sources:1 of
msgid ""
"Plane waves of point sources at infinity seen by a pupil sampled on "
"``grid``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.point_sources:3 of
msgid "Spatial pupil grid."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.point_sources:4 of
msgid "One wavelength (modes are wavefronts) or several (modes are wavecubes)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.point_sources:5
#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.point_sources:6 of
msgid ""
"Directions of the ``M`` sources (angles from the optical axis in the x-z "
"and y-z planes)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.point_sources:7 of
msgid ""
"Power of each source collected by the grid (per spectral channel for "
"several wavelengths)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.point_sources:8 of
msgid "Spectral weights (several wavelengths only)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.point_sources:9 of
msgid "Weights of the modes in the incoherent sum."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.point_sources:10 of
msgid "Optional Jones vector or state name making polarised modes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.unpolarized:1 of
msgid ""
"Natural light with the spatial and spectral content of a scalar "
"``signal``: two orthogonal modes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.unpolarized:3 of
msgid ""
"The power of ``signal`` is split equally between the H and V "
"polarisations, which do not interfere."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.field:1 of
msgid "Complex amplitudes of the modes, shape ``(M, *mode_shape)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.n_modes:1 of
msgid "Number of modes ``M``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.mode_weights:1 of
msgid "Weights of the modes in the incoherent sum (a copy)."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.grid:1 of
msgid "Common grid of the modes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.polarized:1 of
msgid "Whether the modes hold Jones components."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.polychromatic:1 of
msgid "Whether the modes are wavecubes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.power_unit:1 of
msgid "Normalisation of the modes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.intensity_unit:1 of
msgid "Unit of :attr:`intensity`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.members:1 of
msgid "Iterate over the modes."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.mode_intensity:1 of
msgid ""
"Intensity of each mode (spectrally integrated for wavecubes), shape ``(M,"
" ny, nx)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.intensity:1 of
msgid "Incoherent sum :math:`\\sum_m v_m I_m`, shape ``grid.shape``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.power:1 of
msgid "Power of each mode (spectrally integrated for wavecubes), shape ``(M,)``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.total_power:1 of
msgid "Weighted total power :math:`\\sum_m v_m P_m`."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.map:1 of
msgid ""
"Apply ``function`` (member signal -> member signal) to every mode and "
"bundle the results."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.with_power_unit:1 of
msgid "Return the same light in another power unit."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.tilt:1 of
msgid "Tilt every mode by the same angles."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.to_backend:1 of
msgid "Return the same bundle held by backend ``name``."
msgstr ""

#: lumos.fields.incoherent.IncoherentBundle.to_json:1 of
